+
+**Checkpoint**: Baselines recorded; the two canonical locations are confirmed exhaustive; nothing else to initialize.
+
+---
+
+## Phase 2: Foundational (Blocking Prerequisites)
+
+**Purpose**: Everything both tables must share, fixed once, so US1–US3 implement against one normative form
+
+**⚠️ CRITICAL**: No user story work can begin until this phase is complete
+
+- [X] T004 Copy the normative target from `specs/001-bench/contracts/table-contract.md` §1 (target rows table) and §2 (adjacent note) into the working brief: the five target rows with per-file right-cell variants, the new-row placement rule ("new row sits between the bounded-code-change row and the new-public-surface row"), the verbatim adjacent-note text, and the preserved-asymmetry list — file: specs/001-bench/contracts/table-contract.md (read-only reference; output is the shared brief used by T005–T014)
+
+**Checkpoint**: One shared normative target in hand — the two files will be edited against the same wording, which is what SC-005 later verifies.
+
+---
+
+## Phase 3: User Story 1 - Route inert config-value edits to the light row (Priority: P1) 🎯 MVP
+
+**Goal**: The light row of both published tables limits itself to *inert* config values (FR-001, FR-002), so a display-only default still routes to "nothing beyond the summary" and nothing else does for free.
+
+**Independent Test**: From either published table alone, read the light row: every config mention on it is qualified as *inert*, and a display-only default example routes to the lightest route with no ambiguity (spec US1 Independent Test / Acceptance Scenarios 1–2; quickstart Scenario A).
+
+### Implementation for User Story 1
