+## Dependencies & Execution Order
+
+### Phase Dependencies
+
+- **Setup (Phase 1)**: No dependencies - can start immediately
+- **Foundational (Phase 2)**: Depends on Setup completion - BLOCKS all user stories
+- **User Stories (Phases 3–5)**: All depend on Foundational (Phase 2). US1 and US2 are implementation-independent and may run in parallel (different files); US3 is validation-only and depends on US1 + US2 edits being in place in BOTH files
+- **Polish (Phase 6)**: Depends on all desired user stories being complete
+
+### User Story Dependencies
+
+- **User Story 1 (P1)**: Can start after Foundational (Phase 2) - No dependencies on other stories
+- **User Story 2 (P2)**: Can start after Foundational (Phase 2); no dependency on US1's task (different rows/locations), both draw on the same Phase 2 normative brief
+- **User Story 3 (P3)**: Depends on US1 AND US2 edits landing in both files — it is the cross-file consistency proof (SC-005) and fails loudly if either file drifted
+
+### Within Each User Story
+
+- Light-row qualification (US1) before validation reads (US3)
+- New row (T007/T008) before its mention on the expanded row (T009/T010) keeps a reader never facing a dangling obligation during review
+- Adjacent note (T011/T012) pairs with the new row since the note defines terms (inert, behavioural evidence) the new row uses
+- Cross-file tasks inside a story must both land before US3's T013–T015 run
+
+### Parallel Opportunities
+
+- T002, T003 (Setup) in parallel after T001
+- **T005 ∥ T006** (same edit, two files)
+- **T007 ∥ T008** and **T009 ∥ T010** and **T011 ∥ T012** (each pair: same change, different file)
+- Within US2, all six tasks touch disjoint rows/regions of the two files — a two-lane split (one lane per file) can run the whole phase concurrently
+- **T014 ∥ T015** (US3 reads) in parallel after T013; **T016 ∥ T017 ∥ T018** (Polish checks) in parallel
+
