+## Implementation Strategy
+
+### MVP First (User Stories 1–2 on both files)
+
+1. Complete Phase 1: Setup (baselines recorded)
+2. Complete Phase 2: Foundational (normative target in hand)
+3. Complete Phases 3–4: US1 + US2 (the actual delivered prose)
+4. **STOP and VALIDATE**: run quickstart Scenarios A–C against both files
+5. The spec's "MVP" is the two-file table change itself; US3 is its acceptance proof and is nearly free once both files are edited
+
+### Incremental Delivery
+
+1. Setup + Foundational → baselines and normative target locked
+2. Add US1 (light-row inert qualification) → validate Scenario A per file
+3. Add US2 (new row + expanded row + adjacent note) → validate Scenario C probes
+4. Add US3 (consistency validation) → Scenarios B/D/E pass in full
+5. Each increment leaves the repository in a readable state; only the final state claims the feature complete
+
+### Delivery weight (self-reference, per research R-7)
+
+This change is a bounded docs edit: under the tables as they will read after delivery it routes to the **three-line card** in the PR body — the paths (`AGENTS.md`, `docs/process/DELIVERY.md`), the promise (the two published tables carry the contract's config routing and identical adjacent note), and the proving command (quickstart Scenario A greps + `git diff --stat` per Scenario D). No gate, no checker, no `keel.yaml` change (FR-006).
